# Component Discipline

- Components are single-purpose. If a component file exceeds approximately 200 lines, flag it and propose a split — do not block progress, but do not continue adding to the file without surfacing the concern.
- Selection state, understanding state, and domain filter state are owned by App.jsx or a single React context. Components receive them as props or via context — they do not maintain their own copies in local state.
- Do not prop-drill more than 2 levels. If a value needs to reach a deeply nested component, lift state or use context.
- No component directly reads from or writes to localStorage. localStorage access is encapsulated in src/lib/understanding.js and the layout cache logic in App.jsx only.
